tat—that; buddhi—by intelligence; grāhyam—accessible;
atīndriyam—transcendental; vetti—one knows; yatra—wherein; na—never;
ca—also; eva—certainly; ayam—he; sthitaḥ—situated; calati—moves;
tattvataḥ—from the truth; yam—that which; labdhvā—by attainment;
ca—also; aparam—any other; lābham—gain; manyate—considers; na—never;
adhikam—more; tataḥ—than that; yasmin—in which; sthitaḥ—being situated;
na—never; duḥkhena—by miseries; guruṇā api—even though very difficult;
